From 5e18471fb42b9b14c45f6fb5f1c27bf086fa0593 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:25:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 334/371] pirates: a ship launched from the rowboat is offered
 to friends and crew again; Crew and Friends boarding ticks go back on when it
 comes out (board-ticks, AI only)

His brother's ship never showed up in his rowboat lists. The four boarding ticks (setAllowCrewState / Friend /
Guild / Public) are `required broadcast ram ownsend` in pirates.dc with no `db`, so they are never saved with the
ship. When the UberDOG activates a ship from the database, Astron fills every required field the row lacks with its
dc default, 0 for these bools, after PlayerShipAI.__init__ had set Crew and Friends on. Nothing else on the AI sets
them (only the captain's own Boarding Permissions panel), so every launched ship came out with every tick off and
DistributedDinghyAI's friend and crew lists left it out for everyone.

- PlayerShipAI.announceGenerate puts Crew and Friends back on (b_set, so the games see it too) every time a ship
  comes out. Guild and Public stay off, as in the original game. A change the captain makes on the panel still holds
  while the ship stays out. No dc change, no client publish.

AI only; needs an AI restart. Ships already out keep 0 until they are put away and launched again. Test:
test_board_ticks.py (the real PlayerShipAI.__init__, the four required fields filled from their real pirates.dc
defaults, the real announceGenerate, the real DistributedDinghyAI lists): live FAIL 4/7 (ticks 0, brother offered
nothing), patched PASS 7/7.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 pirates/ship/PlayerShipAI.py | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pirates/ship/PlayerShipAI.py b/pirates/ship/PlayerShipAI.py
index 4a0f26a..a3e66e0 100644
--- a/pirates/ship/PlayerShipAI.py
+++ b/pirates/ship/PlayerShipAI.py
@@ -19,6 +19,16 @@ class PlayerShipAI(DistributedShipAI):
         self.allowGuildState = False
         self.allowPublicState = False
 
+    def announceGenerate(self):
+        DistributedShipAI.announceGenerate(self)
+        # family server (11-20): the four boarding ticks are "required" fields that are never saved, so a ship that
+        # comes out of the database arrives with every tick off (Astron fills a missing required field with its dc
+        # default, 0), whatever __init__ set above. His crewmates' and his brother's rowboats then never offered his
+        # ship. Each time the ship comes out it starts from the original ticks again: Crew and Friends on. A change
+        # he makes on the ship's panel still holds while it stays out.
+        self.b_setAllowCrewState(True)
+        self.b_setAllowFriendState(True)
+
     def setAllowCrewState(self, allowCrewState):
         self.allowCrewState = allowCrewState
 
